The register primer passes TABLES, an unpacked array of a class derived from
uvm_reg, to a formal declared as an unpacked array of uvm_reg. An unpacked
array is assignment compatible only with one whose element type is equivalent
(IEEE 1800-2023 7.6, 6.22.2), and a derived class is not equivalent to its
base, so the call is refused. Copy the handles into an array of uvm_reg and
pass that, the form the example already uses on its other branch; what the
register model is configured with is unchanged.

Not sent to the suite, since UVM 1.2 is a closed Accellera release.

--- a/examples/simple/registers/primer/reg_model.sv
+++ b/examples/simple/registers/primer/reg_model.sv
@@ -221,7 +221,12 @@
 	DATA.configure(INDEX, r, this, null);
       end
 `else
-      DATA.configure(INDEX, TABLES, this, null);
+      begin
+         uvm_reg r[256];
+         foreach (TABLES[i])
+            r[i] = TABLES[i];
+         DATA.configure(INDEX, r, this, null);
+      end
 `endif
      
       DATA.build();
